ft. The FW 200 was also known to the Allies as the Courier and Churchill called it the \"Scourge of the Atlantic\" due to its contribution to the heavy Allied shipping losses during the Battle of Atlantic. The aircraft was manufactured between 1937-1944 and 276 were built, including quite a few variants.","LocalizedString":"The Focke-Wulf Fw 200 Condor was a German four engined aircraft, developed as a long range airliner in 1937. During WWII military versions were put into service by the Luftwaffe and the Japanese Navy Air force as a long range reconnaissance aircraft, but also as an anti-shipping, maritime patrol bomber and transport aircraft. The FW 200 was also known to the Allies as the Courier and Churchill called it the \"Scourge of the Atlantic\" due to its contribution to the heavy Allied shipping losses during the Battle of Atlantic. The aircraft was manufactured between 1937-1944 and 276 were built, including quite a few variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Blitz","EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"hasBlitz":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/DontUseOrTemp/fw200condor.fw200condor","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Bot","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FW_200_CONDOR.FW_200_CONDOR","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":342.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fw_200_condor_photo","SourceString":"Fw 200 Condor C1 variant in flight, date unknown. ","LocalizedString":"Fw 200 Condor C1 variant in flight, date unknown. "},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":